{
  "_about": "How a news title names a country (risk-engine.md §5.10, engine 1.3.0). The ISO 3166-1 English short, common and official names come from pycountry at run time; this file adds everyday aliases (as in jobs/analyse/data/countries.tsv), the adjective / demonym ('Chinese firms') and the capital used as a stand-in for the government ('Beijing protests'). Aliases written in capitals (US, UK, UAE) match only in capitals, so the word 'us' is not the United States. 'exclude' lists phrases that contain a country word but do not mean the country ('South China Sea', 'Indian Ocean'); they compete in the same longest-match-first pass, so 'Papua New Guinea' still names the country. Written for this project from general knowledge; codes and country names are factual data.",
